1
00:03:36,879 --> 00:03:37,520
Bro.

2
00:03:37,879 --> 00:03:39,680
You're in for telecom fraud too, right?

3
00:03:44,439 --> 00:03:45,360
The food here is terrible.

4
00:03:45,360 --> 00:03:46,520
There's no spice in it at all.

5
00:03:48,000 --> 00:03:49,400
Bro, where are you from?

6
00:03:49,840 --> 00:03:50,879
You wouldn't know even if I told you.

7
00:03:51,719 --> 00:03:52,639
Lingchuan County.

8
00:03:55,879 --> 00:03:57,039
You're from Lingchuan County too?

9
00:03:59,240 --> 00:04:00,319
Do you know Fang Quan?

10
00:04:01,120 --> 00:04:02,400
Even if our county is small,

11
00:04:02,400 --> 00:04:03,840
I couldn't possibly know everyone.

12
00:04:11,840 --> 00:04:12,800
Fang Quan?

13
00:04:13,479 --> 00:04:14,199
Is he a friend of yours?

14
00:04:14,680 --> 00:04:16,439
He worked at the parts factory over there.

15
00:04:17,720 --> 00:04:19,000
Oh, the parts factory.

16
00:04:19,519 --> 00:04:20,759
My cousin used to work there too.

17
00:04:21,040 --> 00:04:22,040
They had to work from dawn to dusk.

18
00:04:22,040 --> 00:04:24,160
Always rushing around just to eat or use the bathroom.

19
00:04:24,240 --> 00:04:25,839
If you got sleepy and dozed off,

20
00:04:25,839 --> 00:04:27,480
your hand would get chopped right off by the machine.

21
00:04:27,600 --> 00:04:29,160
Then the factory would just kick you out.

22
00:04:29,879 --> 00:04:31,839
They really are a Heartless bunch.

23
00:04:46,720 --> 00:04:47,480
Let me do it.

24
00:04:48,439 --> 00:04:49,680
Okay, thanks, bro.

25
00:04:55,120 --> 00:04:56,120
Are you okay?

26
00:04:56,319 --> 00:04:56,959
I'm fine.

27
00:04:57,360 --> 00:04:58,319
It's just a bit gross.

28
00:05:00,240 --> 00:05:01,360
You seem pretty used to it.

29
00:05:04,439 --> 00:05:05,879
We only do this when we're on duty.

30
00:05:08,040 --> 00:05:10,439
But my mom does this out there every day.

31
00:05:35,120 --> 00:05:35,839
Hello?

32
00:05:36,319 --> 00:05:37,319
Get to the hospital quickly.

33
00:05:37,639 --> 00:05:38,839
Lu's father isn't going to make it!

34
00:05:39,240 --> 00:05:39,959
What did you say?

35
00:05:42,319 --> 00:05:44,319
Old Lu, wake up.

36
00:05:45,160 --> 00:05:47,120
Old Lu, please wake up.

37
00:05:48,519 --> 00:05:49,279
What happened?

38
00:05:49,279 --> 00:05:50,600
My poor Old Lu.

39
00:05:50,600 --> 00:05:51,800
There was no one at home.

40
00:05:51,920 --> 00:05:53,360
I don't know how he fell.

41
00:05:53,360 --> 00:05:55,360
By the time he was found, he was already...

42
00:05:56,199 --> 00:05:58,079
You can't go.

43
00:05:58,680 --> 00:06:00,079
How am I going to explain this to Little Yong?

44
00:06:00,079 --> 00:06:00,800
Lu's mother.

45
00:06:02,279 --> 00:06:02,959
Please sit down.

46
00:06:03,480 --> 00:06:04,439
Lu's mother.

47
00:06:06,439 --> 00:06:09,000
My poor Old Lu.

48
00:06:09,279 --> 00:06:12,199
How could he abandon the two of us?

49
00:06:13,560 --> 00:06:14,759
He just left...

50
00:06:15,079 --> 00:06:16,399
...just like that.

51
00:06:17,279 --> 00:06:20,360
How do I explain this to Little Yong?

52
00:06:22,560 --> 00:06:23,959
When Old Lu was brought in for emergency treatment,

53
00:06:24,160 --> 00:06:25,920
he was holding onto this the whole time.

54
00:06:27,519 --> 00:06:29,279
They said he was trying to reach for this photo

55
00:06:29,279 --> 00:06:30,439
when he fell out of bed.

56
00:07:02,000 --> 00:07:03,199
Lao Kong told me

57
00:07:03,199 --> 00:07:04,759
about Xiao Lu's father.

58
00:07:06,199 --> 00:07:07,120
Are you

59
00:07:07,759 --> 00:07:09,879
trying to get the Detention Center to release him

60
00:07:10,480 --> 00:07:12,600
to attend his father's memorial service?

61
00:07:17,319 --> 00:07:18,319
As for me,

62
00:07:19,000 --> 00:07:21,199
I'd advise you not to waste your effort.

63
00:07:22,000 --> 00:07:23,720
If Xiao Lu gets out right now,

64
00:07:23,720 --> 00:07:25,600
it will only shake his resolve.

65
00:07:26,279 --> 00:07:28,160
Besides, the higher-ups have explicitly told you

66
00:07:28,160 --> 00:07:29,720
to wrap it up quickly.

67
00:07:30,639 --> 00:07:31,519
So,

68
00:07:32,120 --> 00:07:33,360
at a time like this, you really shouldn't

69
00:07:33,360 --> 00:07:34,240
be causing trouble for us

70
00:07:34,560 --> 00:07:36,040
and Zhao Yijie,

71
00:07:36,399 --> 00:07:37,160
okay?

72
00:07:57,879 --> 00:07:58,680
And this

73
00:07:59,519 --> 00:08:00,720
is a little something from me.

74
00:08:02,480 --> 00:08:04,040
Please pass it on to Lu's mother.

75
00:08:30,519 --> 00:08:31,319
Little Yong.

76
00:08:33,759 --> 00:08:34,559
Mom.

77
00:08:35,120 --> 00:08:36,639
Why do you look so tired?

78
00:08:37,039 --> 00:08:38,639
Didn't you say the new job was easy?

79
00:08:41,039 --> 00:08:41,960
I'm not tired.

80
00:08:42,279 --> 00:08:43,159
Mom was moving,

81
00:08:43,320 --> 00:08:44,200
that's why I'm tired.

82
00:08:45,720 --> 00:08:47,080
Let me show you pictures of the new house.

83
00:08:47,360 --> 00:08:47,879
Look.

84
00:08:48,720 --> 00:08:49,799
This is our new home.

85
00:08:49,919 --> 00:08:50,320
This...

86
00:08:50,559 --> 00:08:51,480
This is the kitchen.

87
00:08:51,639 --> 00:08:52,639
See? The furniture and all...

88
00:08:52,960 --> 00:08:53,600
It's all there.

89
00:08:56,600 --> 00:08:57,559
I can see it.

90
00:08:59,440 --> 00:09:01,120
Why isn't Dad in the photos?

91
00:09:05,200 --> 00:09:07,080
The results of the psychiatric evaluation are out.

92
00:09:07,679 --> 00:09:08,519
You are perfectly normal.

93
00:09:08,879 --> 00:09:09,679
At the time of the incident,

94
00:09:09,720 --> 00:09:11,600
your actual age was only 13.

95
00:09:11,720 --> 00:09:12,440
Under the Criminal Law,

96
00:09:12,440 --> 00:09:13,399
in a situation like yours,

97
00:09:13,399 --> 00:09:15,320
you may face massive civil compensation,

98
00:09:15,480 --> 00:09:17,159
but won't bear criminal liability.

99
00:09:20,679 --> 00:09:21,480
However,

100
00:09:22,240 --> 00:09:24,159
starting from March of last year,

101
00:09:24,159 --> 00:09:25,399
the Criminal Law Amendment

102
00:09:25,519 --> 00:09:27,000
has established further provisions.

103
00:09:27,440 --> 00:09:28,919
Even if you are 13,

104
00:09:29,799 --> 00:09:31,519
if the Supreme People's Procuratorate approves it

105
00:09:31,519 --> 00:09:33,759
and determines this case involves aggravated circumstances,

106
00:09:34,519 --> 00:09:36,200
you will still bear criminal liability.

107
00:09:37,039 --> 00:09:38,480
If it really comes to that,

108
00:09:39,399 --> 00:09:41,639
it means fixed-term imprisonment of at least 10 years or life imprisonment,

109
00:09:42,240 --> 00:09:43,600
or even the death penalty.

110
00:09:44,399 --> 00:09:45,200
The death penalty?

111
00:09:45,559 --> 00:09:47,120
That's not what he said before!

112
00:09:49,000 --> 00:09:50,360
Who told you otherwise?

113
00:09:50,559 --> 00:09:51,639
And what exactly did he say?

114
00:09:54,480 --> 00:09:55,759
"Little Yong is only 13.

115
00:09:55,879 --> 00:09:57,399
He won't have to pay with his life for murder."

116
00:10:01,879 --> 00:10:02,559
Of course,

117
00:10:03,000 --> 00:10:03,960
I will try my best

118
00:10:03,960 --> 00:10:05,519
to prevent the worst-case scenario.

119
00:10:05,639 --> 00:10:06,879
But as your defense counsel,

120
00:10:06,879 --> 00:10:08,120
both the best and worst-case scenarios...

121
00:10:08,120 --> 00:10:09,679
I have an obligation to tell you.

122
00:10:09,840 --> 00:10:10,799
Then it will be up to you,

123
00:10:11,519 --> 00:10:12,120
Lu Zhiyong,

124
00:10:12,840 --> 00:10:13,440
to make a decision.

125
00:10:13,440 --> 00:10:14,559
Decide what?

126
00:10:18,000 --> 00:10:18,639
He is still a child.

127
00:10:18,639 --> 00:10:19,879
Talk to me if there's anything.

128
00:10:24,240 --> 00:10:25,960
You really need to reflect on your actions.

129
00:10:26,759 --> 00:10:27,440
You have no idea

130
00:10:27,440 --> 00:10:29,039
how hard it is for your mother out there.

131
00:10:29,879 --> 00:10:31,840
She didn't just get this tired from moving.

132
00:10:32,320 --> 00:10:34,080
She's actually tired from taking care of your father.

133
00:10:35,559 --> 00:10:36,919
And I am sorry to tell you

134
00:10:38,240 --> 00:10:39,679
that your father passed away three days ago.

135
00:10:39,720 --> 00:10:40,559
Lawyer Ding!

136
00:10:45,399 --> 00:10:46,519
And the people you grit your teeth

137
00:10:46,759 --> 00:10:48,279
and desperately try to protect

138
00:10:49,279 --> 00:10:51,000
wouldn't even let me fight for

139
00:10:51,000 --> 00:10:52,480
a brief release for you

140
00:10:52,600 --> 00:10:54,799
so you could attend your father's cremation.

141
00:10:57,039 --> 00:10:58,000
So, Lu Zhiyong,

142
00:10:59,759 --> 00:11:01,759
is what you're going through really worth it?

143
00:11:03,440 --> 00:11:04,639
Think about it carefully.

144
00:11:21,559 --> 00:11:22,360
Lawyer Ding.

145
00:11:23,440 --> 00:11:24,639
Have some water and calm down.

146
00:11:24,759 --> 00:11:25,600
We're all just

147
00:11:25,799 --> 00:11:26,480
concerned about the kid.

148
00:11:27,039 --> 00:11:27,720
Thank you for your trouble.

149
00:11:27,919 --> 00:11:29,200
Fan Dong barging in last time

150
00:11:29,200 --> 00:11:29,960
was a special exception I made.

151
00:11:32,559 --> 00:11:33,320
Thank you.

152
00:11:42,519 --> 00:11:43,919
Take care of yourself in there.

153
00:11:44,559 --> 00:11:45,799
Mom will wait for you to come out.

154
00:12:17,879 --> 00:12:19,279
Hello, I'm here to pick up my phone.

155
00:12:19,279 --> 00:12:20,039
Ding Ning.

156
00:12:21,960 --> 00:12:22,759
Thank you.

157
00:12:32,240 --> 00:12:33,399
Hello.

158
00:12:33,679 --> 00:12:34,399
Hello.

159
00:12:34,799 --> 00:12:36,519
I'm a police officer from the Zhongshan Road Police Station.

160
00:12:37,320 --> 00:12:38,679
Do you know Mr. Yu Songfan?

161
00:12:41,559 --> 00:12:42,080
Thanks.

162
00:12:43,240 --> 00:12:43,919
For what?

163
00:12:43,919 --> 00:12:44,639
Let me tell you,

164
00:12:44,639 --> 00:12:46,799
their whole enforcement process was problematic.

165
00:12:46,879 --> 00:12:48,080
Forgetting my ID

166
00:12:48,240 --> 00:12:48,960
is absolutely not

167
00:12:48,960 --> 00:12:50,919
a reason for them to restrict my freedom.

168
00:12:50,919 --> 00:12:52,159
Alright, stop complaining.

169
00:12:52,360 --> 00:12:53,320
Where did you park the car?

170
00:12:54,799 --> 00:12:55,759
The parking lot.

171
00:12:55,919 --> 00:12:57,080
Where else would I park it?

172
00:12:57,080 --> 00:12:58,440
Okay, then let's go to the parking lot.

173
00:12:59,039 --> 00:13:00,159
I already told you,

174
00:13:00,240 --> 00:13:02,200
I just drove out to buy groceries.

175
00:13:02,279 --> 00:13:02,840
And as a result,

176
00:13:02,840 --> 00:13:04,559
I ran into that cop checking IDs.

177
00:13:04,559 --> 00:13:05,080
I didn't have it on me,

178
00:13:05,080 --> 00:13:06,120
so they called you.

179
00:13:06,919 --> 00:13:08,799
You drove just to buy groceries?

180
00:13:09,639 --> 00:13:10,480
And they also said

181
00:13:10,480 --> 00:13:11,759
you got lost.

182
00:13:12,240 --> 00:13:13,360
You didn't look right,

183
00:13:13,360 --> 00:13:15,080
and couldn't remember your ID number,

184
00:13:15,200 --> 00:13:17,000
so they kindly took you to the station.

185
00:13:17,000 --> 00:13:18,000
Then they looked through your phone,

186
00:13:18,000 --> 00:13:18,799
found my phone number,

187
00:13:18,799 --> 00:13:19,519
and asked me to come pick you up.

188
00:13:19,519 --> 00:13:20,519
Forget it, let's drop it.

189
00:13:20,519 --> 00:13:22,039
Stop talking about it, please.

190
00:13:22,159 --> 00:13:23,159
You're making it sound like

191
00:13:23,159 --> 00:13:25,039
I really can't take care of myself.

192
00:13:25,559 --> 00:13:27,399
Alright, alright, they made a mountain out of a molehill.

193
00:13:27,399 --> 00:13:28,679
It's not your fault, alright?

194
00:13:28,960 --> 00:13:29,840
What about your hand?

195
00:13:30,600 --> 00:13:31,879
When are you getting the stitches out?

196
00:13:31,919 --> 00:13:32,480
It's fine.

197
00:13:32,480 --> 00:13:33,639
Just superficial wounds. It's nothing.

198
00:13:34,879 --> 00:13:36,639
Let's just find the car first, okay?

199
00:13:36,639 --> 00:13:38,279
Stop talking to me.

200
00:13:38,639 --> 00:13:39,799
I can't be answering your questions

201
00:13:39,799 --> 00:13:41,759
while trying to find the car.

202
00:13:41,759 --> 00:13:43,480
I'm telling you, it's on this floor.

203
00:13:43,480 --> 00:13:44,600
Alright, alright, I won't speak.

204
00:13:44,600 --> 00:13:45,639
I won't say a word, okay?

205
00:13:47,960 --> 00:13:48,600
I'm telling you,

206
00:13:48,600 --> 00:13:50,240
I remember it's definitely on this floor.

207
00:14:14,759 --> 00:14:16,440
Do you remember which color it was?

208
00:14:46,080 --> 00:14:46,639
Here.

209
00:14:49,480 --> 00:14:50,519
I told you.

210
00:14:50,639 --> 00:14:51,480
I remember.

211
00:14:51,679 --> 00:14:52,320
Right, right, right.

212
00:14:52,320 --> 00:14:52,799
It's right here.

213
00:14:52,879 --> 00:14:53,679
Alright, found it.

214
00:14:53,679 --> 00:14:55,480
This parking lot's layout is just terrible.

215
00:14:55,480 --> 00:14:56,080
Seriously.

216
00:14:56,080 --> 00:14:56,759
Here, let me drive.

217
00:14:58,039 --> 00:14:59,039
I want to practice driving.

218
00:14:59,039 --> 00:15:00,159
I haven't driven in a long time.

219
00:15:00,159 --> 00:15:01,720
It's not like I have Parkinson's.

220
00:15:02,120 --> 00:15:03,200
I can drive myself.

221
00:15:03,320 --> 00:15:04,039
I know.

222
00:15:04,039 --> 00:15:05,399
I just want some practice.

223
00:15:05,399 --> 00:15:06,519
You can be my instructor.

224
00:15:19,799 --> 00:15:22,080
The investigation won't happen overnight.

225
00:15:22,720 --> 00:15:24,600
You still need to get some rest.

226
00:15:28,799 --> 00:15:30,519
I know you're having a hard time.

227
00:15:31,759 --> 00:15:33,279
If there's anything you want to say,

228
00:15:33,799 --> 00:15:34,600
just tell me.

229
00:15:36,799 --> 00:15:38,039
Right by that supermarket.

230
00:15:38,320 --> 00:15:39,320
Pull over up ahead.

231
00:15:43,080 --> 00:15:44,399
I'll go buy some bread

232
00:15:44,399 --> 00:15:45,759
for Awu's breakfast tomorrow.

233
00:15:45,759 --> 00:15:46,759
He has school.

234
00:15:48,919 --> 00:15:50,320
Awu is at Zhao Yijie's house.

235
00:16:39,720 --> 00:16:41,039
I always thought

236
00:16:43,200 --> 00:16:45,600
even if I forgot everything,

237
00:16:48,519 --> 00:16:50,919
the people and things important to me,

238
00:16:50,919 --> 00:16:51,559
I would

239
00:16:53,080 --> 00:16:55,039
keep etched in my mind.

240
00:16:57,279 --> 00:16:58,480
But now...

241
00:17:01,360 --> 00:17:02,200
I know

242
00:17:03,879 --> 00:17:05,279
there will come a day

243
00:17:06,519 --> 00:17:07,920
when I see Awu

244
00:17:08,240 --> 00:17:10,279
and won't remember who he is.

245
00:17:10,839 --> 00:17:12,599
I'll forget Awu's name,

246
00:17:12,599 --> 00:17:14,119
forget him entirely,

247
00:17:14,319 --> 00:17:16,279
and eventually forget you, too.

248
00:17:18,519 --> 00:17:20,279
Don't be so pessimistic.

249
00:17:23,039 --> 00:17:24,880
I know I don't have much time left.

250
00:17:26,599 --> 00:17:28,920
Before I forget everything,

251
00:17:28,920 --> 00:17:31,039
I need to make sure you're settled.

252
00:17:36,039 --> 00:17:36,599
Lao Yu,

253
00:17:37,319 --> 00:17:38,119
don't worry.

254
00:17:39,160 --> 00:17:40,880
If that day really comes,

255
00:17:41,839 --> 00:17:43,119
Awu and I will both be just fine.

256
00:17:43,119 --> 00:17:43,920
Trust me.

257
00:17:45,440 --> 00:17:46,519
I trust you.

258
00:17:47,559 --> 00:17:50,039
And I believe you'll take good care of Awu.

259
00:17:51,319 --> 00:17:53,400
But I don't trust Zhao Yijie.

260
00:17:55,039 --> 00:17:55,960
You know?

261
00:17:57,720 --> 00:17:59,559
I'm just afraid that one day,

262
00:17:59,559 --> 00:18:01,279
I'll forget that bastard.

263
00:18:01,559 --> 00:18:04,200
Forget all the evil he's done.

264
00:18:05,039 --> 00:18:07,119
I wish I could personally

265
00:18:07,119 --> 00:18:09,680
strike the gavel to judge him.

266
00:18:12,079 --> 00:18:13,920
But I know I won't live to see that day.

267
00:18:26,319 --> 00:18:28,119
I really thought about killing him.

268
00:18:28,599 --> 00:18:30,279
And then killing Bi Wenhao, right?

269
00:18:31,079 --> 00:18:31,519
Think about it.

270
00:18:31,519 --> 00:18:32,400
You know the law.

271
00:18:32,400 --> 00:18:33,079
You know

272
00:18:33,079 --> 00:18:35,799
the court can't possibly try a sick man like me.

273
00:18:37,359 --> 00:18:38,880
They can't do anything to me.

274
00:18:39,400 --> 00:18:40,559
Fine, even if it means

275
00:18:40,559 --> 00:18:42,319
spending the rest of my life in prison,

276
00:18:42,480 --> 00:18:43,480
so what?

277
00:18:44,720 --> 00:18:45,680
My mind

278
00:18:46,359 --> 00:18:48,559
is already a complete mess.

279
00:18:48,680 --> 00:18:50,319
In a prison, in a nursing home,

280
00:18:50,319 --> 00:18:52,799
or anywhere else, it makes no difference.

281
00:18:52,839 --> 00:18:55,119
I can no longer undo my mistakes.

282
00:18:55,279 --> 00:18:56,400
Most importantly,

283
00:18:59,039 --> 00:19:01,480
I'll even forget who I am.

284
00:19:03,839 --> 00:19:06,359
